        <briefdescription>
<para>Get the computer&apos;s public address via DNS. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The public address is the address of the computer from the point of view of the internet, i.e. something like 89.54.1.169 or 2600:1901:0:13e0::1 as opposed to a private or local address like 192.168.1.56 or fe80::1234:5678:9abc. It is necessary for communication with hosts outside of the local network.</para>
<para>The only way to reliably get the public address is to send data to a host on the internet and see what the origin address is; as a consequence, this function depends on both your network connection and the server, and may be very slow. You should try to use it as little as possible. Because this function depends on the network connection and on a distant server, you can specify a time limit if you don&apos;t want your program to get stuck waiting in case there is a problem; this limit is deactivated by default.</para>
<para>This function makes use of DNS queries get the public address.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>timeout</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Maximum time to wait, <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput> to wait forever </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>type</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of public address to get</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Public IP address of the computer on success, <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput> otherwise </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
